WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:11.440
The names change, the feeling is always the
same. It's always you loving more, you

00:11.440 --> 00:20.240
waiting more, you giving more than you
get, right? And in the end, you sitting on the floor

00:20.240 --> 00:26.480
asking yourself, what's wrong
with me? There's nothing wrong with you,

00:26.880 --> 00:32.720
but there's something no one taught you,
and that's exactly what I came to talk about

00:32.720 --> 00:39.760
today. Stay here with me until the end, because
I'm going to tell you something I never

00:39.760 --> 00:46.860
really told anyone this way.
It's the story of the devastating breakup I

00:46.860 --> 00:56.260
had. I was once a woman who loves too much,
and I don't wish that on anyone. I suffered

00:56.260 --> 01:03.100
so much with the end of a relationship,
to the point of crying every day for six

01:03.100 --> 01:09.620
months, can you believe it? In the first week the
sadness was so great that I got

01:09.620 --> 01:17.860
pneumonia from so much suffering. I got sick,
my body collapsed with me. All I wanted

01:17.860 --> 01:26.440
was to die, truly. And I'll
explain why. My whole life was

01:26.440 --> 01:32.560
turned toward him. All my plans
involved him. All my purpose revolved

01:32.560 --> 01:38.460
around that relationship. And when
he ended it with me, there was

01:38.460 --> 01:48.120
absolutely nothing left. On top of that, my
mother had just passed away. So

01:48.120 --> 01:55.720
everything was taken from me at once. It was as if
they'd ripped away not just the ground under me, but

01:55.720 --> 01:59.460
a piece of my heart. It hurt
physically.

02:02.180 --> 02:08.360
And you know what was worse? I thought I'd never
love anyone again. And at the same

02:08.360 --> 02:14.740
time I was terrified just imagining
going through that again. I look

02:14.740 --> 02:21.520
back, today I see it. When he left,
I didn't exist. I didn't even know why

02:21.520 --> 02:24.780
I was alive. I had lost myself way
too much.

02:28.460 --> 02:36.040
I only recovered about a year
after that breakup. And when I

02:36.040 --> 02:40.780
recovered, I swore to myself. Like,
never, never would I go through that

02:40.780 --> 02:49.520
again. But I didn't swear it the way
you're thinking. I didn't swear I'd never

02:49.520 --> 02:55.660
give myself again, never want to love
again. I didn't close my heart. That's

02:55.660 --> 03:01.920
what everyone does. And it doesn't heal.
It only stiffens you, only hardens you. What

03:01.920 --> 03:06.760
I swore was, I'm going to understand. I'm going
to find out what happened inside

03:06.760 --> 03:13.420
me to turn me into that woman I no
longer recognized. And then the work began.

03:15.780 --> 03:21.380
I'll be honest with you. It wasn't
pretty, it wasn't easy. Because when I

03:21.380 --> 03:27.240
looked inside, I didn't find a poor little
victim who deserved to be loved better.

03:29.260 --> 03:33.520
I found my neediness, my
emotional dependence.

03:35.940 --> 03:44.680
And that's what hurts. So pay attention. We
think we love too much. But actually,

03:44.960 --> 03:50.660
we don't love too much. Because we're
in a lack of love. And that's the biggest

03:50.660 --> 03:56.740
confusion there is. The people who are
called women, or even men, who

03:56.740 --> 04:05.820
love too much, are actually in a lack of
love. They don't love too much. I always say

04:05.820 --> 04:11.240
that these people write a bad check
of love. That is, they don't have what to

04:11.240 --> 04:15.260
give. They give what they'd like to
receive.

04:18.180 --> 04:23.220
I was like a little bird with its mouth
open waiting for food. Food

04:23.220 --> 04:30.700
that would never reach my mouth. And
when I saw that, it was the turning point. I

04:30.700 --> 04:37.180
learned to let go. I learned to set the
other free. I learned to say no. To set

04:37.180 --> 04:44.300
limits. To exist for myself again.
Because I discovered something. When you

04:44.300 --> 04:51.040
only exist for the other, you stop
existing. You cancel your desires. You cancel

04:51.040 --> 04:57.280
your goals. And that behavior
costs you dearly. You lose respect for

04:57.280 --> 05:04.600
yourself. Now you must be thinking. Ah, here's
the catch. So you healed, you loved yourself and

05:04.600 --> 05:15.640
the perfect prince came. No. What came was the
hardest relationship of my life. I

05:15.640 --> 05:19.700
met the man of my life. And he didn't
love me.

05:23.040 --> 05:30.580
He'd look at me and say it in plain
words. I don't feel the same as you. I

05:30.580 --> 05:39.660
don't want the same as you. A year and a half.
A year and a half I lived with a man who

05:39.660 --> 05:46.780
didn't love me back. And look at the work
I had to do. Look at the drastic

05:46.780 --> 05:52.000
change. Because the woman I was before
would have done emotional blackmail. Would have

05:52.000 --> 05:59.420
humiliated herself. Would have become the little bird with
its mouth open again. But I'd already done

05:59.420 --> 06:05.140
the work. So I did something that
seems impossible.

06:07.200 --> 06:15.020
I accepted his right not to love me. I
didn't force it. I didn't chase. I didn't try

06:15.020 --> 06:21.180
to convince anyone to love. Because I'd
already learned. Love is an energy that

06:21.180 --> 06:29.660
goes out. I love. But neediness isn't love.
Neediness is the lack of love that looks

06:29.660 --> 06:36.680
like love. And the other person feels that
difference. So I came back to myself. I

06:36.680 --> 06:41.960
went on with my life. I stayed
whole. I did love, but I didn't die.

06:42.240 --> 06:49.020
I didn't paralyze. I didn't beg. And
when the time came. And this part is

06:49.020 --> 06:55.680
important. I didn't stay there forever
accepting crumbs. I loved myself

06:55.680 --> 07:03.120
enough not to accept crumbs
forever. So I gave an ultimatum. Truly.

07:03.380 --> 07:09.360
It wasn't blackmail. It was truth. Either we
walk together. Or I go on with my life. And

07:09.360 --> 07:17.420
I really do. And then. That's when he
chose me. Not when I begged. Not

07:17.420 --> 07:23.660
when I blackmailed. Not when I seduced.
Not when I erased myself. But when I

07:23.660 --> 07:30.460
was whole enough. To leave if I
needed to. Today we've been married for 12

07:30.460 --> 07:39.160
years. And he's not just my love. He's
my best friend. We're not against

07:39.160 --> 07:41.840
each other. We're together. Against the world.

07:45.260 --> 07:52.840
Now I need you to understand why
I told you all this. Because the difference

07:52.840 --> 07:59.220
between the woman who cried six months on
the floor and the woman who's married in peace for 12

07:59.220 --> 08:04.820
years wasn't luck. It wasn't the right man.
It wasn't the right man. It wasn't a formula

08:04.820 --> 08:15.220
